{"title":"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problem 32","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A mathematical set is a collection of elements which satisfy a specified condition or conditions and braces {} are used to indicate a set. Which of the following is the set of all positive prime numbers between one and ten?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25eb17c9adaeb3cb0d41f791f0ade742489174b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)} \\quad \\{2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af12e5892816e1b9d30f06e266bcb9d88ad69ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(B)} \\quad \\{2, 3, 6, 9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c23cdb33ade97c4dc0011dd235e6ad91e67ce019.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(C)} \\quad \\{2, 4, 6, 8\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae9d97fd7b4791fe5509bad4970b9c948d4c60f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(D)} \\quad \\{2, 3, 5, 7\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/5/98524f954f1afd20e21043249910c894f2f5597e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(E)} \\quad \\{3, 5, 7, 9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The primes between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff3e93cc98d2eaa04bec7bea0273c471161b4570.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/43420adcd0fce9dce3978d53b97a8e0262b58da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc93afd012d6af697c4fae71d14de49f021d78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Mathematics_Contests\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Mathematics Contests\">1963 TMTA High School Mathematics Contests</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems\">Problems</a>)</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_31\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problem 31\"> Problem 31</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"40%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=TMTA_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_Past_Problems/Solutions\" title=\"TMTA High School Mathematics Contest Past Problems/Solutions\">TMTA High School Mathematics Contest Past Problems/Solutions</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_33\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problem 33\">Problem 33</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018041629\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 79/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 661/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 305/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1898/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.355      1 Template:Succession_box\n100.00%    6.355      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20676:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018041629 and revision id 144637. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}